2025-07-01 14:14:37,289 - openai._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-58e07c9c-48c4-4d67-add4-f4d0e4f8626a', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Based on the following units of competency\n\nCourse Context and Goals:\nThis course is designed for adult learners in a vocational education setting. The focus is on practical, hands-on learning with real-world applications. Students should develop both theoretical understanding and practical skills that can be immediately applied in the workplace.\n, generate a brief course overview (2-3 paragraphs):\n\n- ICTAII401: This unit describes the skills and knowledge required to identify opportunities where artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML) and deep learning (DL) can be applied to support the automation of work tasks and improve organisational productivity\n\nThe overview should:\n- Explain what students will learn\n- Describe the key skills and knowledge areas\n- Mention the practical applications\n- Be written in a professional but accessible tone\n- Align with the course context and goals provided\n\nCourse Overview:'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Course Overview:\n\nIn the ICTAII401 unit, students will delve into the transformative world of artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML), and deep learning (DL) within a vocational education setting. This course offers a comprehensive introduction to the concepts and principles guiding these cutting-edge technologies. Students will gain a theoretical understanding of how AI, ML, and DL can be harnessed to automate work tasks, leading to increased organizational efficiency and productivity. The course is tailored for adult learners, emphasizing practical and hands-on learning experiences that ensure immediate applicability in professional environments.\n\nThroughout the course, learners will acquire key skills including identifying AI opportunities, evaluating the potential impact of ML techniques, and understanding the intricacies of DL applications. By engaging in real-world scenarios and projects, participants will learn to leverage these technologies to optimize workflows and contribute valuable insights to their organizations. The focus on practical applications ensures that students are not only proficient in theoretical knowledge but also adept at implementing AI-driven solutions that address tangible business challenges. Through this approach, students will be well-equipped to support innovation and drive productivity in their respective vocational fields.', 'refusal': None}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Based on the following units of competency\n\nCourse Context and Goals:\nThis course is designed for adult learners in a vocational education setting. The focus is on practical, hands-on learning with real-world applications. Students should develop both theoretical understanding and practical skills that can be immediately applied in the workplace.\n, generate a 20-week course structure with weekly topics:\n\n- ICTAII401: This unit describes the skills and knowledge required to identify opportunities where artificial intelligence (AI), machine learning (ML) and deep learning (DL) can be applied to support the automation of work tasks and improve organisational productivity\n\nFor each week, provide:\n1. A clear topic title\n2. 3-5 key learning points\n3. An appropriate in-class activity\n\nConsider the course context and goals when designing topics and activities.\n\nFormat the response as a JSON array with objects containing:\n- week: week number\n- title: topic title\n- topics: array of learning points\n- activity: in-class activity description\n\nResponse:'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '```json\n[\n    {\n        "week": 1,\n        "title": "Introduction to AI, ML, and DL",\n        "topics": [\n            "Define AI, ML, and DL and the differences between them",\n            "Understand the historical context and evolution of AI technologies",\n            "Identify current trends and future prospects in AI applications"\n        ],\n        "activity": "Group discussion on notable AI advancements and their implications in various industries"\n    },\n    {\n        "week": 2,\n        "title": "AI, ML, and DL in the Workplace",\n        "topics": [\n            "Explore how AI, ML, and DL can enhance workplace productivity",\n            "Identify common tasks that can be automated using AI",\n            "Examine case studies of AI implementation in different sectors"\n        ],\n        "activity": "Case study analysis and presentation on an organization using AI for task automation"\n    },\n    {\n        "week": 3,\n        "title": "Understanding Data: The Foundation of AI",\n        "topics": [\n            "Learn about different types of data and their significance in AI",\n            "Explore data collection and preprocessing techniques",\n            "Understand the concept of big data and its role in ML and DL"\n        ],\n        "activity": "Hands-on lab session on data collection and preprocessing"\n    },\n    {\n        "week": 4,\n        "title": "Basic Algorithms in Machine Learning",\n        "topics": [\n            "Introduction to core ML algorithms (e.g., regression, classification)",\n            "Understand the importance of model selection and evaluation",\n            "Explore overfitting and underfitting in model development"\n        ],\n        "activity": "Workshop on implementing basic ML algorithms using a simple dataset"\n    },\n    {\n        "week": 5,\n        "title": "Deep Learning Fundamentals",\n        "topics": [\n            "Introduction to neural networks and how they work",\n            "Understand the architecture of a neural network",\n            "Explore use cases of deep learning in various industries"\n        ],\n        "activity": "Interactive session on building 